<% title "#{@cohort.name} — roster" %>

<%# FUIME: the roster board. The one screen to watch during an event.

    It answers "who is stuck, and on what?" for everybody at once, which is a
    different question from either existing admin queue: admin/applications asks
    whether a venture should exist and admin/operator_vetting whether it may
    sell, both one row at a time. Nobody works a queue during an event — they
    walk the room looking for the four people who cannot get past something.

    The Next step column is the whole point of the page. See
    Fuime::FounderProgress for why it names one action rather than a state. %>

<% progresses = @applications.map { |a| Fuime::FounderProgress.new(application: a) } %>
<% by_stage = progresses.group_by(&:stage) %>

<h1><%= @cohort.name %></h1>

<p class="muted">
  Code <code><%= @cohort.code %></code> ·
  <%= progresses.size %> of <%= @cohort.max_members %> ·
  <% if @cohort.admitting? %>
    <span class="success">admitting</span>
  <% else %>
    <span class="muted"><%= @cohort.admission_blocker %></span>
  <% end %>
  · expires <%= @cohort.expires_at.to_fs(:long) %>
</p>

<%# ── The funnel, counted ───────────────────────────────────────────────────

    Read left to right it is the founder's journey, and the first column with a
    number smaller than the one before it is where the room is stuck. That is the
    fastest possible read of fifty people and it is why these are counts rather
    than a chart. %>
<div class="card mb2">
  <h2 class="mt0 text-lg">Where everyone is</h2>
  <div class="flex flex-row flex-wrap gap-4">
    <% Fuime::FounderProgress::STAGES.each_with_index do |stage, i| %>
      <%# Cumulative: somebody who has sold has also been vetted. A per-stage
          count would show 1 at "vetted" once everybody moved past it, which
          reads as a collapse rather than progress. %>
      <% reached = progresses.count { |p| Fuime::FounderProgress::STAGES.index(p.stage) >= i } %>
      <div>
        <div class="text-lg"><strong><%= reached %></strong></div>
        <div class="muted text-sm"><%= stage.to_s.humanize %></div>
      </div>
    <% end %>
  </div>
</div>

<%# ── Parents, tracked separately and deliberately ──────────────────────────

    Not part of the funnel above, because under merchant-of-record a guardian
    does not block selling — it blocks being PAID
    (Fuime::PayableAssessment). Folding it into the funnel would have organisers
    chasing parents on the day instead of chasing first sales, which is the wrong
    order for everybody. It still has to be visible, because money cannot move
    until it is done. %>
<% awaiting_parent = progresses.select(&:guardian_pending?) %>
<div class="card mb2">
  <h2 class="mt0 text-lg">Parents</h2>
  <% if awaiting_parent.any? %>
    <p class="mb1">
      <strong><%= awaiting_parent.size %></strong> of <%= progresses.size %> have no
      guardian on the account yet. They can sell today; they can't be paid out
      until a parent accepts.
    </p>
    <p class="muted text-sm mb0">
      <%= awaiting_parent.map { |p| p.founder.name }.join(", ") %>
    </p>
  <% else %>
    <p class="muted mb0">Everyone who needs a guardian has one.</p>
  <% end %>
</div>

<%# ── The roster ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── %>

<div class="card mb2">
  <h2 class="mt0 text-lg">Founders</h2>

  <% if progresses.any? %>
    <table class="w-full">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Founder</th>
          <th>Business</th>
          <th>Stage</th>
          <th>Next step</th>
          <th>Parent</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <%# Stuck first. During an event the people who are fine do not need to be
            at the top of anything — sorting by funnel position puts the rows
            somebody has to act on where they will be seen. %>
        <% progresses.sort_by { |p| Fuime::FounderProgress::STAGES.index(p.stage) }.each do |p| %>
          <tr>
            <td><%= p.founder.name %><br><span class="muted text-sm"><%= p.founder.email %></span></td>
            <td>
              <% if p.event %>
                <%= link_to p.event.name, event_path(p.event) %>
              <% else %>
                <span class="muted"><%= p.application.name.presence || "—" %></span>
              <% end %>
            </td>
            <td>
              <% if p.done? %>
                <span class="success"><%= p.stage.to_s.humanize %></span>
              <% else %>
                <%= p.stage.to_s.humanize %>
              <% end %>
            </td>
            <td class="<%= "muted" if p.done? %>"><%= p.next_action %></td>
            <td>
              <% if p.guardian_pending? %>
                <span class="muted">Waiting</span>
              <% else %>
                ✓
              <% end %>
            </td>
          </tr>
        <% end %>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  <% else %>
    <p class="muted">Nobody has used this code yet.</p>
  <% end %>
</div>

<%# ── Turning it off ────────────────────────────────────────────────────── %>

<div class="card">
  <h2 class="mt0 text-lg">The code</h2>
  <p class="muted text-sm">
    Created by <%= @cohort.created_by.name %>. Their stated basis, recorded on
    every business this code admits:
  </p>
  <blockquote class="muted"><%= @cohort.rationale %></blockquote>

  <% unless @cohort.archived? %>
    <%= button_to "Turn this code off", cohort_archive_admin_index_path(@cohort),
                  method: :post, class: "danger",
                  form: { data: { turbo_confirm: "Turn off #{@cohort.code}? Nobody new can join. Founders already admitted keep their businesses." } } %>
  <% else %>
    <p class="muted mb0">Turned off <%= @cohort.archived_at.to_fs(:long) %>.</p>
  <% end %>
</div>
